<li id="bib.bib84" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">Zhong et al. (2023)</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
Wanjun Zhong, Lianghong Guo, Qiqi Gao, He Ye, and Yanlin Wang.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">Memorybank: Enhancing large language models with long-term memory, 2023.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.10250" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.10250</a>.

</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib85" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">Zhou et al. (2025)</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
Zijian Zhou, Ao Qu, Zhaoxuan Wu, Sunghwan Kim, Alok Prakash, Daniela Rus, Jinhua Zhao, Bryan Kian Hsiang Low, and Paul Pu Liang.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">Mem1: Learning to synergize memory and reasoning for efficient long-horizon agents, 2025.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.15841" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.15841</a>.

</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib86" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">Zhu et al. (2025)</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
Rui-Jie Zhu, Tianhao Peng, Tianhao Cheng, Xingwei Qu, Jinfa Huang, Dawei Zhu, Hao Wang, Kaiwen Xue, Xuanliang Zhang, Yong Shan, et al.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">A survey on latent reasoning.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib86.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">arXiv preprint arXiv:2507.06203</em>, 2025.

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Additional Related Works</h2>

<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">LLM Decoding &amp; RL.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Two additional topics that relate to our work are LLM decoding and reinforcement learning (RL). From the <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">decoding perspective</span>, <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">MemGen</span> dynamically generates and inserts latent tokens, which shares similarity with speculative decoding where a drafter model receives the current decoding context and produces subsequent drafted tokens <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cai et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fu et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2025b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Goel et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.
. However, these methods primarily aim to accelerate LLM inference, whereas <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">MemGen</span> focuses on leveraging latent states as effective carriers of memory.
From the <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RL perspective</span>, <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">MemGen</span> employs rule-based RL to train the memory trigger, which is closely related to reinforcement learning with variable reward (RLVR), including GRPO from DeepSeek-R1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI et al., 2025</a>)</cite> and its various derivatives <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qian et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2025a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wei et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.
While there exist efforts combining RL with agent memory, to our knowledge, most do not address self-improving memory; for example, MemAgent <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib76" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al., 2025</a>)</cite> and MEM1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib85" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al., 2025</a>)</cite> focus on handling long-context inputs rather than evolving memory mechanisms.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Optimization Algorithm on Memory Weaver</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide a detailed exposition of the optimization algorithms for training the memory weaver, <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{\text{weaver}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mtext>weaver</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{\text{weaver}}</annotation></semantics></math>, as mentioned in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Memory Weaver: Synthesizing and Inserting Latent Memory ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ MemGen: Weaving Generative Latent Memory for Self-Evolving Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>. The core principle, as established in <a href="#S4.E10" title="In Training Recipe. ‣ 4.3 Memory Weaver: Synthesizing and Inserting Latent Memory ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ MemGen: Weaving Generative Latent Memory for Self-Evolving Agents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, is to update only the weaver’s parameters, denoted as <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, while keeping the reasoner <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> frozen. This modularity allows <span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">MemGen</span> to be compatible with various optimization paradigms. We detail the specific implementations for Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT) and a reinforcement learning approach, Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO).</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Combining <span id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">MemGen</span> with SFT</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The objective of Supervised Fine-Tuning is to train the memory weaver to generate latent memories that guide the frozen reasoner <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> to replicate the behavior observed in a dataset of high-quality demonstration trajectories. We leverage the provided history of past experiences, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}=\{(x_{i},\tau_{i}^{*})\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}=\{(x_{i},\tau_{i}^{*})\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is treated as an expert demonstration.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Each expert trajectory <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of a sequence of states and actions, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i}^{*}=(s_{i,0},a_{i,0}^{*},s_{i,1},a_{i,1}^{*},\ldots)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i}^{*}=(s_{i,0},a_{i,0}^{*},s_{i,1},a_{i,1}^{*},\ldots)</annotation></semantics></math>. Each expert action <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i,t}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i,t}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sequence of tokens, <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i,t}^{*}=(\mathbf{z}_{i,t,1}^{*},\mathbf{z}_{i,t,2}^{*},\ldots,\mathbf{z}_{i,t,L_{t}}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i,t}^{*}=(\mathbf{z}_{i,t,1}^{*},\mathbf{z}_{i,t,2}^{*},\ldots,\mathbf{z}_{i,t,L_{t}}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>. The goal is to maximize the conditional log-likelihood of generating these expert token sequences.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">During the training of the weaver, both the reasoner <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and the memory trigger <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> are held fixed. At each token generation step <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> where the trigger activates, the weaver <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{\theta^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{\theta^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> takes the reasoner’s hidden states <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}_{i,t,&lt;j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}_{i,t,&lt;j}</annotation></semantics></math> as input and produces a latent memory <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>. The reasoner then generates the next token conditioned on this memory. The SFT objective is to adjust the weaver’s parameters <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to maximize the probability of the ground-truth token <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{i,t,j}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{i,t,j}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Formally, the optimization problem is to minimize the negative log-likelihood of the expert trajectories, averaged over the dataset <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. The loss function for the weaver’s parameters <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A2.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{SFT}}(\theta^{\prime})=-\mathbb{E}_{(x_{i},\tau_{i}^{*})\sim\mathcal{H}}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T_{i}-1}\sum_{j=1}^{L_{t}}\log\pi_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{i,t,j}^{*}\mid s_{i,t},\mathbf{z}_{i,t,&lt;j}^{*},\mathbf{M}_{i,t,j})\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐳</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{SFT}}(\theta^{\prime})=-\mathbb{E}_{(x_{i},\tau_{i}^{*})\sim\mathcal{H}}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T_{i}-1}\sum_{j=1}^{L_{t}}\log\pi_{\theta}(\mathbf{z}_{i,t,j}^{*}\mid s_{i,t},\mathbf{z}_{i,t,&lt;j}^{*},\mathbf{M}_{i,t,j})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where the latent memory <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{i,t,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{i,t,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is synthesized by the weaver at that specific step:</p>
<table id="A2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{i,t,j}=\mathcal{W}_{\theta^{\prime}}(\mathbf{H}_{i,t,&lt;j})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{i,t,j}=\mathcal{W}_{\theta^{\prime}}(\mathbf{H}_{i,t,&lt;j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Note that the generation of <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{i,t,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{i,t,j}</annotation></semantics></math> only occurs if the fixed trigger <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> determines an invocation is needed at step <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. In steps where no memory is invoked, the conditioning term <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}_{i,t,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}_{i,t,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is omitted.
The gradients are computed exclusively with respect to the weaver’s parameters <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and used to update them via gradient descent:</p>
<table id="A2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}\leftarrow\theta^{\prime}-\eta\nabla_{\theta^{\prime}}\mathcal{L}_{\text{SFT}}(\theta^{\prime})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}\leftarrow\theta^{\prime}-\eta\nabla_{\theta^{\prime}}\mathcal{L}_{\text{SFT}}(\theta^{\prime}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is the learning rate. Through this process, the memory weaver learns to synthesize latent memories that effectively steer the frozen reasoner’s generative process to align with the training data’s behavior, thereby internalizing the knowledge from the demonstration data without corrupting the general capabilities of the core LLM.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Combing <span id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">MemGen</span> wirh GRPO</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The memory weaver can also be trained using a reinforcement learning objective. We specifically adapt the GRPO algorithm.
The training process begins by sampling a batch of tasks from the experience history <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each task <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the policy <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\theta}^{\mathcal{W}_{\theta^{\prime}},\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\theta}^{\mathcal{W}_{\theta^{\prime}},\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> (composed of the frozen reasoner <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and the current memory weaver <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}_{\theta^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}_{\theta^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>) to generate a group of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> distinct trajectories, denoted as <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{i}=\{\tau_{i,1},\tau_{i,2},\ldots,\tau_{i,K}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{i}=\{\tau_{i,1},\tau_{i,2},\ldots,\tau_{i,K}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each trajectory is generated by the agent’s interaction with the environment and results in a final reward <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\tau_{i,k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\tau_{i,k})</annotation></semantics></math>, evaluated by the reward function. Going forward, GRPO computes a group-relative baseline by averaging the rewards of all trajectories within the group <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{R}(\mathcal{G}_{i})=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}R(\tau_{i,k})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{R}(\mathcal{G}_{i})=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}R(\tau_{i,k}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The advantage for a specific trajectory <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i,k}</annotation></semantics></math> is then its reward relative to this baseline:</p>
<table id="A2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\tau_{i,k})=R(\tau_{i,k})-\bar{R}(\mathcal{G}_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\tau_{i,k})=R(\tau_{i,k})-\bar{R}(\mathcal{G}_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This formulation allows the weaver to learn by differentiating between better and worse outcomes within a set of its own generations, promoting policies that produce trajectories with above-average rewards. The final objective function, maximized with respect to the weaver’s parameters <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, is:</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\small\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta^{\prime})=\mathbb{E}_{x_{i}\sim\mathcal{H},\,\mathcal{G}_{i}\sim\Pi_{\theta}^{\mathcal{W}_{\theta^{\prime}},\mathcal{T}}}\left[\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}A(\tau_{i,k})\log\Pi_{\theta}^{\mathcal{W}_{\theta^{\prime}},\mathcal{T}}(\tau_{i,k}\mid x_{i})-\beta\,\text{KL}\left(\Pi_{\theta}^{\mathcal{W}_{\theta^{\prime}},\mathcal{T}}(\cdot\mid x_{i})\parallel\Pi_{\text{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{i})\right)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒥</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">GRPO</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℋ</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒢</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">∼</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒲</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒯</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mi mathsize="0.900em">K</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">K</mi></munderover><mi mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒲</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒯</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">β</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒲</mi><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒯</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext mathsize="0.900em">ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\small\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}(\theta^{\prime})=\mathbb{E}_{x_{i}\sim\mathcal{H},\,\mathcal{G}_{i}\sim\Pi_{\theta}^{\mathcal{W}_{\theta^{\prime}},\mathcal{T}}}\left[\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}A(\tau_{i,k})\log\Pi_{\theta}^{\mathcal{W}_{\theta^{\prime}},\mathcal{T}}(\tau_{i,k}\mid x_{i})-\beta\,\text{KL}\left(\Pi_{\theta}^{\mathcal{W}_{\theta^{\prime}},\mathcal{T}}(\cdot\mid x_{i})\parallel\Pi_{\text{ref}}(\cdot\mid x_{i})\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a fixed reference policy and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is a coefficient controlling the strength of the KL regularization. The gradients are computed only for the weaver’s parameters <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, thus refining its ability to synthesize impactful latent memories while preserving the integrity of the core reasoner.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Training Dataset Setup</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all datasets except PopQA, we utilize their official training sets to train both the <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">memory weaver</span> and <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">memory trigger</span>. Specifically, we first train the memory weaver in isolation. Since the trigger module is not yet available at this stage, latent memory tokens are randomly inserted at punctuation marks during training to provide diverse learning signals. Once the memory weaver is adequately trained, we proceed to train the memory trigger, enabling it to learn when to invoke memory (with the memory weaver fixed). For PopQA, as it lacks a dedicated training set, we instead leverage the trained model on TriviaQA (whose tasks are similar to PopQA) and directly evaluate on PopQA.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Parameter Configurations</h3>

<figure id="A3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Hyperparameters used in the training of MemGen.</figcaption>
<table id="A3.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A3.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Settings</span></td>
<td id="A3.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyperparameters</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T2.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T2.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training (SFT)</span></td>
<td id="A3.T2.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T2.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_text"></span><span id="A3.T2.2.2.2.2" class="ltx_text">
<span id="A3.T2.2.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="A3.T2.2.2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A3.T2.2.2.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">train_batch_size = 4</span></span>
<span id="A3.T2.2.2.2.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A3.T2.2.2.2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">learning_rate = 1e-5</span></span>
<span id="A3.T2.2.2.2.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A3.T2.2.2.2.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">epochs = 2</span></span>
<span id="A3.T2.2.2.2.2.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A3.T2.2.2.2.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">warmup_ratio = 0.1</span></span>
<span id="A3.T2.2.2.2.2.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A3.T2.2.2.2.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">optim = adamw_torch</span></span>
<span id="A3.T2.2.2.2.2.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A3.T2.2.2.2.2.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">schedular = cosine</span></span>
</span></span><span id="A3.T2.2.2.2.3" class="ltx_text"></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T2.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.T2.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T2.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training (GRPO)</span></td>
<td id="A3.T2.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T2.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_text"></span><span id="A3.T2.2.3.2.2" class="ltx_text">
<span id="A3.T2.2.3.2.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="A3.T2.2.3.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A3.T2.2.3.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">rollout_batch_size = 8</span></span>
<span id="A3.T2.2.3.2.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A3.T2.2.3.2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">train_batch_size = 8</span></span>
<span id="A3.T2.2.3.2.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
